<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Post purchase retention</h2>
<p>Define each message by purpose and channel before enabling post purchase retention automation. Recheck current permission, opt-outs, complaints, bounces, order state, and support or return state at send time across every sender. Necessary order and service messages follow their own rules; adding an offer requires a separate marketing eligibility decision.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented permission</td><td>Hold optional marketing until eligibility for its purpose and channel is established</td><td>A purchase, form submission, or email permission alone does not establish SMS permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Eligible, never purchased</td><td>Deliver the promised asset; enroll only in the ongoing content actually requested</td><td>One-time fulfillment and recurring marketing have separate purposes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Check the current cart, order state, channel eligibility, and global suppression before a reminder</td><td>Queued reminders can become stale before delivery</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Exit reminders for the purchased cart; evaluate care, education, and later offers independently</td><td>A purchase ends that recovery job, not every separately eligible journey</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Pause optional selling during open cases; preserve necessary service</td><td>Case closure does not automatically restore marketing eligibility</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Review clicks, purchases, bounces, complaints, and preferences before sunsetting</td><td>Non-opening alone does not establish inactivity</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS permission present</td><td>Verify current SMS eligibility, quiet hours, caps, and opt-outs separately</td><td>Email permission does not transfer to SMS</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Use recorded account preferences, buying role, and applicable terms</td><td>B2B status alone proves neither permission nor a contract restriction</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Use actual bounce and abuse signals; apply proportionate verification</td><td>A free-domain address alone does not establish poor quality or ineligibility</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Exclude QA identities from live marketing and outcome reporting</td><td>Test activity must not inflate commercial results</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Apply the same documented eligibility and suppression rules</td><td>Inferred identity does not justify an untracked exception</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Hold uncertain records; investigate evidence before any repermission request</td><td>Repermission is itself a message requiring an eligible channel and purpose</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
